id: transformation
name: Transformation
type: standard
actionCost: 1
kiCost: 0
attacking: false
requiresTarget: false
tags: transformation
# Forms, Enhancements and their Aspects are not built yet (the user's ruling, 2026-10-03): the Transformation and its
# Stress Test Requirement are asked, the Stress Test rolled from its window (1d10 + Stress Bonus) and settled on the card
# (chat.mjs askTransformation / postTransformation). Failed: Stress Exhaustion, "as per the rules on Stress Tests".
# Made: entering it - and what entering it does (Legend Realized, Burst Limit), leaving a Form or an Enhancement for it,
# the Tier of Power Requirement - is the table's until Transformations exist. Tagged `transformation`, so Stress
# Exhaustion's "you cannot enter any Enhancement or Form" refuses it. Exploitable only with the Long Transformation
# Aspect - not built either, so none.
transforms: true
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Roll the Stress Test for a Form or Enhancement: made, you enter it; failed, Stress Exhaustion.
text: >
  Transformation Maneuver: Enter a Transformation!
  –Maneuver Type: Standard
  –Action Cost: 1 Action
  –KP Cost: N/A
  –Exploitable: N/A (Unless that Transformation has the Long Transformation Aspect — see Aspects).
  –Effect: Roll the Stress Test for a Form or Enhancement you have access to and meet the Tier of Power Requirements
  for. If you match or exceed the Stress Test Requirement, you enter the Transformation and apply any effects that
  occur when entering that Transformation (such as Legend Realized and Burst Limit). If you fail, you suffer from Stress
  Exhaustion as per the rules on Stress Tests (see: Failing a Stress Test, Transformation Rules).

  If you are already in a Form, you may attempt to transform into another Form or Transcended Enhancement. Upon
  succeeding, before you apply any effects or properly enter this Transformation, leave the Form you were in previously.

  If you are already in an (Non-Transcended) Enhancement, you may attempt to transform into another (Non-Transcended)
  Enhancement. If you do, and have reached the maximum number of Transformations you can use concurrently, upon
  succeeding, before you apply any effects or properly enter this Transformation, leave an Enhancement you were in
  previously.
